{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 30, :comments ["<b>Let me gulp down, I pray.</b> He spoke with foolishness in this expression, and it is from the language of מלעיטין את הגמל (forcing the camel to swallow). And on this the Rabbis, of blessed memory, expounded (Proverbs 13:25): ״צדיק אוכל לשובע נפשו ובטן רשעים תחסר״ — the righteous eats to the satiety of his soul, but the belly of the wicked lacks. Eliezer, the servant of Abraham, said: ״הגמיאיני נא מעט מים״ — 'let me drink, I pray, a little water'; and Esav said: ״הלעיטני נא״ — 'let me gulp down.' 'The righteous eats to the satiety of his soul' — this is Eliezer; 'and the belly of the wicked lacks' — this is Esav." "<b>Of this red, this red.</b> Either the lentils were red, or they were cooked with red spices, and Esav did not know what kind of dish it was and called it 'this red,' and therefore everyone called his name Edom by way of mockery, because he sold a precious birthright for a little of this dish." "<b>And it is fitting</b> to interpret ״מן האדום האדום הזה״ — 'of this red, this red' — as alluding to the matter of reduplication, for the following reason known in the wisdom of the stars: that the planet Mars (כוכב מאדים) has its power over blood and over the sword and over wars; also the red fruits among the species of vegetation draw from its power; and the precious stones among the species of the inanimate that are red, such as garnet (גירגנ״ץ) and ruby (רובי״ן) and the like, are in its portion. And therefore he said: ״הלעיטני נא מן האדום האדום הזה״ — 'let me gulp down, I pray, of this red, this red' — that is, of this red dish which draws power from the red one, namely the planet Mars whose name is Edom (red), under which he was born. And it was his star and his mazal, and therefore he was a shedder of blood, and he was given the blessing of the sword." "<b>By way of the Midrash:</b> ״מן האדום האדום הזה״ — 'of this red, this red.' Resh Lakish said: he is red, his dish is red, his land is red, his warriors are red, their garments are red, the One who exacts retribution from him is red, in red garments. He is red — ״ויצא הראשון אדמוני״ (Genesis 25:25). His dish is red — ״מן האדום האדום הזה״. His land is red — ״ארצה שעיר שדה אדום״ (Genesis 32:4). His warriors are red — ״מגן גבוריהו מאדם״ (Nahum 2:4). Their garments are red — ״ואנשי חיל מתולעים״ (ibid.) — men of valor clad in worm-dye (red). The One who exacts retribution from him is red — ״דודי צח ואדום״ (Song of Songs 5:10). In red garments — ״מדוע אדום ללבושך״ (Isaiah 63:2)."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {3 "The prooftext for 'their garments are red' — ואנשי חיל מתולעים from Nahum 2:4 — refers to warriors clad in scarlet (תולע = worm/crimson dye); the Midrash reads תולעים as relating to red coloring. He writes (שם) 'ibid.' indicating Nahum 2:4 again."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:15:18.118103046Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}